Module trappedway "A way with something laid across it" {
  Place field "a field" is wilderness.
  Place yard "the yard" is room within field at 0, 0.
  Place shed "the shed" is room within field at 1, 0.
  Passage gate "the gate" is path between yard and shed taking 2 minutes.
  Company party "You" of 1 at yard.
  // A wire across the gate, as the deep sites lay their traps: looked at closely, it is understood; understood, it
  // can be cut by whoever knows traps.
  Hazard gate_trap "the tripwire" means "Deal (1d4) piercing damage to ally unless dexterity save against (12).".
  Discovery gate_snare_known "A wire is strung across the gateway at the height of an ankle, and runs off into the hedge to something that would fall.".
  Thing gate_snare "the tripwire" on gate {
    State primed dangerous "Something catches the light low across the gateway: a wire.".
    State sprung "The tripwire has gone off, and is spent.".
    State made_safe "The tripwire is made safe. Whoever goes by now goes by unharmed.".
    Change cut "Cut the wire where it is tied off" from primed to made_safe needing trapwork after learning gate_snare_known.
    Hurts with gate_trap when primed then sprung.
  }
  Observe gate_snare_read beside gate of gate_snare when tried(gate_snare, looking) and state(gate_snare, primed) "A wire is strung across the gateway at the height of an ankle, and runs off into the hedge to something that would fall." teaches gate_snare_known.
  Observe yard_scene at yard when true "A muddy yard, and a gate in the hedge.".
  Observe shed_scene at shed when true "A shed of tarred planks.".
  Goal false.
}
